### This MATLAB script computes the MC quantification using load and position data of the flipper moving in water.
# To run the programme in MATLAB, follow this steps:
  1. Download the .zip file from this GitHub directory.
  2. Open MATLAB desktop or ONLINE version.
  3. Import the .zip file to MATLAB
  4. Decompress the zip file inside your MATLAB directory
  5. Run the file named "MC_MOTOR_sand_2cycles_V2.m". This should create the graphs with the MC values.

  If the struct file ("myStruct_water10.mat") fails, a new struct file will be needed. This can be done as follows:
  1. Double-click on ".CSV" excel file (raw data). Select "type" > Column Vectors, and click on "Import Selection"
  2. Once data imported as column vectors, click on "create_struct.m", and run the script. This should create a new struct file
    in the workspace. Once we have the struct file created in the workspace, we can simply RUN the ".m" file to compute the MC quantification.
  3. If wanted, the struct file can be saved as ".mat" file in the folder, so there is no need to create a new struct every time you open MATLAB.

